            <span class="font-bold text-ink block mb-0.5">{d.mechanismsLabel}</span>
            <p id="desc-mechanisms" class="text-muted">
              Viscous dissipation generates 71% of cooking thermal input via screw flight shear rate of 1,850 s⁻¹. Pseudoplastic shear-thinning (flow index n = 0.38) prevents drive motor torque overload. Starch melting occurs smoothly with zero ungelatinized hard cores.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span class="font-bold text-ink block mb-0.5">{d.mitigationLabel}</span>
            <p id="desc-mitigation" class="text-muted">
              Maintain barrel cooling jacket water flow at Zone 6-7 to stabilize melt temperature at 160°C. Inspect rupture disc burst membrane during scheduled downtime; verify Category 4 safety interlock on hopper chute under OSHA 1910.212.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Mathematical Formulations & Engineering Reference -->
  <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 mb-10 shadow-xs">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4 mb-5">
      <h2 class="text-title-sm font-semibold text-ink">
        {d.scienceTitle}
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">
        {d.scienceSub}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">1. Radial Gap Shear Rate (γ̇)</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          γ̇ = (π · D · N) / (60 · δ)
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Where D is screw flight diameter, N is rotational speed (RPM), and δ is radial clearance. At high RPM and tight clearance, shear rate exceeds 2,500 s⁻¹, driving rapid polymer chain deformation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">2. Ostwald-de Waele Power Law</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          η = K₀ · exp(E_a/RT) · γ̇^(n - 1) · exp(-β·M_w)
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Food melts exhibit strong shear-thinning (n = 0.28 to 0.42). Apparent viscosity collapses under high shear, while low dough moisture (M_w) drives exponential viscosity spikes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">3. Viscous Dissipation Heat (q_diss)</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          q_diss = η · γ̇² · V_shear
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Volumetric mechanical energy dissipation into heat. Scales quadratically with shear rate, providing 60% to 85% of total thermodynamic cooking enthalpy in direct-expanded products.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">4. Specific Mechanical Energy (SME)</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          SME = (2π · τ · N) / (60 · ṁ) = P_shaft / ṁ
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Mechanical work transferred from motor to dough per unit mass (Wh/kg). Critical metric: values above 165 Wh/kg trigger irreversible molecular shearing of amylose polymers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">5. Die Nozzle Hydraulic Pressure (P_die)</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          ΔP_die = (8 · η · L_die · Q) / (π · R_die⁴)
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Die backpressure governed by melt viscosity, volumetric flow Q, and orifice restriction. Inversely proportional to orifice radius to the 4th power; partial blockages produce massive pressure surges.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline/60">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink font-mono mb-1">6. Archard Barrel Abrasive Wear</h4>
        <div class="font-mono text-amber-700 font-bold my-2 p-2 bg-surface rounded text-center border border-hairline/60">
          W_wear = K_abrasion · (F_N · L_sliding) / H_liner
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          Radial flight clearance growth over service hours. Hard bimetallic carbide liners (64 HRC) retard wear by 85% compared to uncoated 4140 steel, preserving pumping and preventing back-leakage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Specifications Comparison Table -->
  <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 mb-10 shadow-xs overflow-x-auto">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4 mb-4">
